  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Women&#x2019;s participation and Influence in Decision Making in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WiPSU seeks to strengthen women&#x2019;s influence in national policies through their active, strategic participation and by enhancing&#x2019;s women&#x2019;s capacities to leverage on positions they currently hold, both at Local and National Government to influence policies to be inclusive of women&#x2019;s human rights (WHR). The project supports women to attain a critical mass to maintain women&#x2019;s representation and voice in governance. 

The project therefore not only, seeks to influence policy but to use the current opportunity in the electoral cycle to support women to participate equally in all electoral processes in the run up to the 2023 elections, in order to retain their quantitative representation both at Parliament and at Local Government level. This retention will ensure that women&#x2019;s voices and influence in policy making is sustained beyond 2023 Zimbabwean harmonised elections.</narrative>
  </description>
